// RUN: cd %corpus && ! %zomc compile --check 08-adt/inherent_method_body_capability_neg_02.zom > %t 2>&1
// RUN: %FileCheck %s --input-file %t

// A scalar `let` local declared inside a receiver method body is well-formed
// source the HIR method gate does not admit. The body checker must recognize
// the local's pattern inside the Method owner (not only Function owners) so
// the method drains per definition as ZOM4099, never as a checker invariant or
// an internal compiler error.

// CHECK-LITERAL: Error [ZOM4099]: this function body uses a construct the compiler cannot generate code for yet
// CHECK-LITERAL:   --> conformance/08-adt/inherent_method_body_capability_neg_02.zom:3:3
